    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Have you ever seen a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "solar panel",
            "zh": "太阳能电池板"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in your neighbourhood? Solar panels "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "convert",
            "ref": "v-convert"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " sunlight into electricity. Over the past ten years, the price of solar panels has gone down greatly. In many parts of the world, solar energy is now the cheapest form of electricity. More and more people have started using solar energy to power their homes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "However, solar panels also have their problems. They stop working at night and on rainy days. Is it possible to make them produce electricity all of the time?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Now, scientists at "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Soochow University",
            "zh": "苏州大学"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in China have invented a new solar panel. It can produce electricity not only from solar energy but also from falling rain. When a raindrop falls on the solar panel and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "rolls",
            "ref": "v-roll"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " down, it creates "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "friction",
            "ref": "v-friction"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on the panel’s surface, which can be converted into electricity."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Sun Baoquan is one of the inventors. “Our "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "device",
            "ref": "v-device"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " can produce electricity in any weather during the day,” he says. “It can even provide electricity at night if there is rain.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The solar panel, however, does not make much electricity from falling rain. So Sun is still working hard to improve it. The scientist also wants to make solar panels more ______. He is trying to build solar panels that are as soft as clothing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The field of solar energy is developing fast. Scientists around the world have been improving solar panels. Some have been working on ways to combine solar panels with wind power. Some have been trying to use sunlight to produce liquid and gas fuels."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
